From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 00:04:13 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 161/179] fix(gastown): cut agent worktrees from the rig's
 default_branch, not origin/HEAD (gcp-8v32)

worktree-setup.sh took the base for a new agent worktree, and for --sync, from
refs/remotes/origin/HEAD. That pointer is per-clone and drifts independently of
the rig's configured default_branch, so on a rig where the two disagree (feryn:
master vs dev; gascity: main vs edge-integration) the script silently cut the
agent from the wrong mainline. `git worktree add -b <branch> <remote-ref>` also
takes the upstream from the start point, so the same line mis-tracked the
branch, and a later `git pull --rebase` replayed the agent's work onto a stale
base. Crew seats are the load-bearing case: they have no workspace-setup step,
so the pre_start worktree is where they work permanently.

The script now accepts `--default-branch <branch>` and both pre_start lines pass
gc's `{{.DefaultBranch}}`, quoted so an empty value survives as an argument.
When the value is non-empty the sync site and the create site resolve the base
with the rule mol-polecat-work's workspace-setup uses: origin/<branch> if it
exists (halting only when the local branch holds commits on no remote, counted
with `rev-list --count ... --not --remotes`, and merely noting a stale one),
else the local branch, else STOP without substituting origin/HEAD. A failed
sync fetch refuses only when origin/<branch> is already known locally. The
disagreement with origin/HEAD is reported once per run. origin/HEAD stays the
fallback when the flag is absent, empty, bare, or an unrendered `{{...}}` left
by a gc that predates the variable. Unknown arguments now exit 2.

Not changed: the reuse path still ignores the start point, so an existing
mis-tracked branch is repointed by `gc doctor session-branch-upstream --fix`,
not here. The city-local copies of the script are city config (gc-57uso).

Validation: nine new cases in test_worktree_setup_sync.sh (RED against the old
script on the HEAD assertion of the first; each of the two NEW arms deleted in
turn fails its own case), test_agent_pre_start_budget.sh pins the new strings,
shellcheck reports nothing beyond the base's SC1007/SC1083.
